{
  "material": "belt_straw",
  "kind": "ground",
  "formula": "ground v4: cover tiled at tile_size_m and at tile_size_m*phi, averaged, stretched 1+bias along the lodging azimuth and rotated to it; soil tiled at its tile_size_m, gained to its albedo_target when given; bare = the asset's patch layout (lib/patches.py): the outlines filled times FLOOR_EDGE + (1 - FLOOR_EDGE) * the ramp of each core filled and blurred with sigma patches.FEATHER_M / 6, so 255 on the outline shrunk by the feather, FLOOR_EDGE at the outline and 0 outside it, mapped u = x / size_m + 0.5, v = z / size_m + 0.5 with v up the image; green = the asset's strips (lib/mat.py) filled and blurred with sigma mat.GREEN_FEATHER_M / 2; strewn masks clamp(2 m - c), c the cover luminance high-passed at STRAW_M, blended with LOBE_M value noise and stretched to 0-1: the bare mask (noise BARE_LOBES), the lip (m = LIP_LEVEL * min(1, 2 * the outlines blurred with sigma LIP_M / 3), noise BARE_LOBES), the gaps between straws (m = sqrt(gap_share / 2), noise GAP_LOBES) and the strips shown (m = GREEN_LEVEL * green, noise GAP_LOBES); relief = the asset's relief (lib/mat.py) sampled on RELIEF_SAMPLES^2 and resized bicubic, h01 in 0-1; albedo = the cover times 1 - RELIEF_TONE (1 - h01) with the straw gain for albedo_target, the strips shown tinted to the green tint, the gaps the cover gained to gap_albedo (the soil without one), the soil under bare and the lip, then a global gain against clipping; normal composited the same with the cover normals rotated by the azimuth; mask R 0, G AO times 1 - RELIEF_AO (1 - h01), B 0, A 1 - roughness; detail albedo = the detail set's diffuse as grey at its size with a linear mean of 0.5; 8-bit sRGB albedos",
